---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About Us — DigitalDramaa"
  description="How DigitalDramaa tracks internet drama, gaming drama, and tech scandals — and how our live, AI-assisted commentary actually works."
  keywords={["DigitalDramaa", "about digitaldramaa", "internet drama site", "AI news commentary", "gaming drama news", "tech scandal news"]}
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
    <h1>About DigitalDramaa</h1>
    <p>Live commentary on internet drama, gaming drama, and tech chaos — refreshed hourly.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>What We Do</h2>
    <p>
      DigitalDramaa tracks the internet's messiest stories as they break — gaming
      leaks, streamer callouts, platform bans, data breaches, and the influencer
      drama that dominates timelines for a day and then disappears. We pull from
      a wide net of gaming, tech, and internet-culture sources, rewrite each
      story in plain language, and add a short, opinionated "Our take" within
      the hour.
    </p>

    <h2>How It Works</h2>
    <p>
      Every article on this site starts as reporting published somewhere else.
      Our system continuously scans a set of gaming, tech, and internet-culture
      feeds, and when a genuinely new story shows up, it's summarized and
      rewritten using AI, then published with a link back to the original
      source. We are not the ones breaking these stories — we're helping you
      catch up on them faster.
    </p>

    <h2>Our Editorial Approach</h2>
    <p>
      The "Our take" section on every article is exactly that — a take, not a
      verdict. Internet drama is often still unfolding when we publish, so our
      commentary reflects where a story stands at that moment, not a final
      conclusion. Claims about real people that are disputed or unconfirmed are
      reported as alleged, not stated as fact, and we link to the original
      reporting on every story so you can always go check the source yourself.
    </p>

    <h2>Transparency</h2>
    <p>
      DigitalDramaa is upfront about what it is: an automated site that uses AI
      to summarize and comment on stories reported elsewhere. We're not a wire
      service and we don't claim original reporting credit for the underlying
      news — our value is speed, organization, and a quick read on why a story
      matters, with a clear path back to the original source for anyone who
      wants the full picture. See our <a href="/terms-and-conditions">Terms & Conditions</a>
      and <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> for more detail, or
      <a href="/contact">contact us</a> with questions or correction requests.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding: var(--sp-32) 0 var(--sp-24);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-32);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--accent-wash);
    padding: 3px 9px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .page-head h1 {
    font-size: 2.4rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.2rem;
  }

  .page-head p {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .prose {
    max-width: 72ch;
    padding-bottom: var(--sp-64);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin: var(--sp-32) 0 0.6rem;
  }

  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .prose p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
